@anon.814f0bdf02fb37ec5ace91213a028c11.771 = private unnamed_addr constant [663 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for uses of `assert False`.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0APython removes `assert` statements when running in optimized mode\0A(`python -O`), making `assert False` an unreliable means of\0Araising an `AssertionError`.\0A\0AInstead, raise an `AssertionError` directly.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aassert False\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Araise AssertionError\0A```\0A\0A## Fix safety\0AThis rule's fix is marked as unsafe, as changing an `assert` to a\0A`raise` will change the behavior of your program when running in\0Aoptimized mode (`python -O`).\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: `assert`](https://docs.python.org/3/reference/simple_stmts.html#the-assert-statement)\0A", align 1
@anon.814f0bdf02fb37ec5ace91213a028c11.772 = private unnamed_addr constant [81 x i8] c"Do not `assert False` (`python -O` removes these calls), raise `AssertionError()`", align 1
@anon.814f0bdf02fb37ec5ace91213a028c11.773 = private unnamed_addr constant <{ ptr, [8 x i8] }> <{ ptr @anon.814f0bdf02fb37ec5ace91213a028c11.772, [8 x i8] c"Q\00\00\00\00\00\00\00" }>, align 8
@anon.814f0bdf02fb37ec5ace91213a028c11.774 = private unnamed_addr constant [26 x i8] c"reuse-of-groupby-generator", align 1
@anon.814f0bdf02fb37ec5ace91213a028c11.775 = private unnamed_addr constant [587 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for multiple usage of the generator returned from\0A`itertools.groupby()`.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AUsing the generator more than once will do nothing on the second usage.\0AIf that data is needed later, it should be stored as a list.\0A\0A## Example:\0A```python\0Aimport itertools\0A\0Afor name, group in itertools.groupby(data):\0A    for _ in range(5):\0A        do_something_with_the_group(group)\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aimport itertools\0A\0Afor name, group in itertools.groupby(data):\0A    values = list(group)\0A    for _ in range(5):\0A        do_something_with_the_group(values)\0A```\0A", align 1
@anon.814f0bdf02fb37ec5ace91213a028c11.776 = private unnamed_addr constant [106 x i8] c"Using the generator returned from `itertools.groupby()` more than once will do nothing on the second usage", align 1
@anon.814f0bdf02fb37ec5ace91213a028c11.777 = private unnamed_addr constant <{ ptr, [8 x i8] }> <{ ptr @anon.814f0bdf02fb37ec5ace91213a028c11.776, [8 x i8] c"j\00\00\00\00\00\00\00" }>, align 8
@anon.814f0bdf02fb37ec5ace91213a028c11.778 = private unnamed_addr constant [26 x i8] c"builtin-variable-shadowing", align 1
@anon.814f0bdf02fb37ec5ace91213a028c11.779 = private unnamed_addr constant [1081 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for variable (and function) assignments that use the same names\0Aas builtins.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AReusing a builtin name for the name of a variable increases the\0Adifficulty of reading and maintaining the code, and can cause\0Anon-obvious errors, as readers may mistake the variable for the\0Abuiltin and vice versa.\0A\0ABuiltins can be marked as exceptions to this rule via the\0A[`lint.flake8-builtins.ignorelist`] configuration option.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Adef find_max(list_of_lists):\0A    max = 0\0A    for flat_list in list_of_lists:\0A        for value in flat_list:\0A            max = max(max, value)  # TypeError: 'int' object is not callable\0A    return max\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Adef find_max(list_of_lists):\0A    result = 0\0A    for flat_list in list_of_lists:\0A        for value in flat_list:\0A            result = max(result, value)\0A    return result\0A```\0A\0A## Options\0A- `lint.flake8-builtins.ignorelist`\0A\0A## References\0A- [_Why is it a bad idea to name a variable `id` in Python?_](https://stackoverflow.com/questions/77552/id-is-a-bad-variable-name-in-python)\0A", align 1
