@anon.814f0bdf02fb37ec5ace91213a028c11.826 = private unnamed_addr constant [864 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for `if` expressions that can be replaced with `bool()` calls.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0A`if` expressions that evaluate to `True` for a truthy condition an `False`\0Afor a falsey condition can be replaced with `bool()` calls, which are more\0Aconcise and readable.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0ATrue if a else False\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Abool(a)\0A```\0A\0A## Fix safety\0A\0AThis fix is marked as unsafe because it may change the program\E2\80\99s behavior if the condition does not\0Areturn a proper Boolean. While the fix will try to wrap non-boolean values in a call to bool,\0Acustom implementations of comparison functions like `__eq__` can avoid the bool call and still\0Alead to altered behavior. Moreover, the fix may remove comments.\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: Truth Value Testing](https://docs.python.org/3/library/stdtypes.html#truth-value-testing)\0A", align 1
