@anon.814f0bdf02fb37ec5ace91213a028c11.986 = private unnamed_addr constant [535 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for comparisons against NaN values.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AComparing against a NaN value can lead to unexpected results. For example,\0A`float(\22NaN\22) == float(\22NaN\22)` will return `False` and, in general,\0A`x == float(\22NaN\22)` will always return `False`, even if `x` is `NaN`.\0A\0ATo determine whether a value is `NaN`, use `math.isnan` or `np.isnan`\0Ainstead of comparing against `NaN` directly.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aif x == float(\22NaN\22):\0A    pass\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aimport math\0A\0Aif math.isnan(x):\0A    pass\0A```\0A\0A", align 1
